From 1043f2e740b1de598bad3f4953b02ef0538277d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:46:52 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: gaokun3 fpcmd: add the Goodix GDIX5125 sensor

Some gaokun3 units carry a Goodix GDIX5125 instead of the FocalTech
FTE7001; the board straps (TLMM GPIO61/62) tell them apart, as the ACPI
_HID of \_SB.SPBA does. Both sit behind the same signed TA, which talks to
a Goodix MCU over SPI with its own request envelope and "Milan" frames.

Add GAOKUN3_FPCMD_IOC_SET_SENSOR, set by user space before INIT; without
it the driver stays on FocalTech, so existing users are unchanged. For
Goodix the fixed ioctls map to:

- INIT: the Windows boot order (version, state, idle, chip ID,
  INIT_FP_DATA1, OTP, idle, mode idle, DAC, configuration, state,
  INIT_FP_DATA2) and a finger-detect reference. DAC, tcode and FDT delta
  come from the unit's own OTP, with the Windows driver's CRC-8 checks
  and its FT, MT and 3-of-4 DAC fallbacks. Windows also tries a saved
  OTP copy and otherwise keeps the template DAC values; there is no
  saved copy here, so INIT fails instead. The configuration template is
  not in the kernel: it is read from
  /vendor/firmware/gaokun3-goodix-cfg.bin, accepted only if it is the
  known type 14 template, and patched from OTP.
- GET_FINGER_STATUS: physical finger presence from the ten FDT areas,
  against a reference that follows slow drift.
- CAPTURE: one image, returned as 36 x 160 little-endian 12-bit samples
  (the three scans of each column averaged, dummy columns dropped). The
  image is ready 100-130 ms after the request; a read before that comes
  back from the TA with result 3 and no data, so the driver waits 100 ms
  and then polls, skipping late replies to earlier commands. The image is
  plaintext: the driver clears its copies once user space has it.
- PROBE and WAKE: version query and NOP.

The MCU sleeps after about 30 s idle and drops the command that wakes it,
so a NOP goes first after 5 s without a command, measured in boot time to
cover suspend. A missing reply, or an image that never arrives, is
reported as -EPROTO.

The protocol helpers are pure functions in gaokun3_fpcmd_goodix.h and are
tested in user space against frames, replies, OTP, configuration and
image data recorded on a Goodix unit. On that unit, with 0001 and 0002,
the driver loads the TA, initialises the sensor in about 0.7 s, follows
finger down and lift-off, captures in about 155 ms, and wakes the MCU
after 40 s idle. The stricter reply checksum, the packet skipping while
polling, the buffer clearing and the bounded configuration read came
after those measurements and are tested offline only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific QSEE transport]
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig                |   9 +-
 drivers/firmware/qcom/gaokun3_fpcmd.h        |  18 +
 drivers/firmware/qcom/gaokun3_fpcmd_goodix.h | 355 ++++++++++++
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_qseecom_fpcmd.c   | 550 ++++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 923 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/firmware/qcom/gaokun3_fpcmd_goodix.h

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig b/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig
index 6bbd841b7..ec919dc6a 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -1,11 +1,16 @@
 config GAOKUN3_FPCMD
-	bool "Gaokun3 FTE7001 restricted fingerprint transport"
+	bool "Gaokun3 FTE7001/GDIX5125 restricted fingerprint transport"
 	depends on QCOM_QSEECOM && QCOM_SCM=y
+	select CRC32
 	default n
 	help
-	  Fixed ioctl transport for the signed FocalTech fingerprint TA.
+	  Fixed ioctl transport for the signed fingerprint TA, driving either
+	  the FocalTech FTE7001 or the Goodix GDIX5125 sensor; user space
+	  selects the variant from the board straps.
 	  Requires the downstream QSEE app-load/shutdown/listener patch.
